# Project context

## Folder responsibilities (do not mix)

| Folder | Use for | Do not use for |
|--------|---------|----------------|
| `context/` | Evergreen stack, decisions, workflow, domain rules (auth, deploy) | Feature specs, tutorials |
| `specs/` | Scoped work: acceptance criteria, what to build now | Permanent stack rules, agent workflow |
| `docs/` | Human onboarding, architecture narrative, ADRs, runbooks | Version pins, task checklists |

Entry point: `AGENTS.md`. Spec overrides chat for **scope**; `context/` overrides for **stack and conventions**.

## Before non-trivial work, read

1. `context/README.md` — bootstrap order and folder map
2. `context/workflow.md` — agent workflow *(when present)*
3. `context/tech-stack.md` — **canonical tech stack** *(when present)*
4. `context/06-stack-responsibilities.md` — stack ownership, CI/CD, env *(when present)*
5. Any matching `specs/*.md` file the user or issue references
6. `context/auth.md` — when implementing authentication, sessions, or protected routes

Stack details: `context/tech-stack.md`. Version floor: `context/00-security-versions.md` (Next.js **16.2.6+**, App Router) *(when present)*.

**GitHub:** `context/07-agentic-github.md` and skill `.cursor/skills/github-ops/`. May commit on feature branches; **never merge PRs**. Production branch: **`master`**.

**Deploy:** `context/05-deploy.md`. Vercel plugin for previews; `npm run validate` before preview deploys.

**Layout:** `frontend/` = Next.js; `backend/services/` = APIs. Never add backend services under `frontend/`. Local Docker: `context/10-local-docker.md`.

Keep changes minimal and run verification commands from the relevant context or spec doc.
